{"name":"Hidden Cove","hex":"#cec6bd","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hidden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["past participle of hide"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Located or positioned out of sight; not visually apparent.","Obscure. (Can we add an example for this sense?)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hidden"},{"term":"cove","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A hollow in a rock; a cave or cavern. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A concave vault or archway, especially the arch of a ceiling."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To arch over; to build in a hollow concave form; to make in the form of a cove."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cove"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cove","blocks":[{"text":"A cove is a small bay or coastal inlet. They usually have narrow, restricted entrances, are often circular or oval, and are often situated within a larger bay. Small, narrow, sheltered bays, inlets, tidal creeks, or recesses in a coast are often considered coves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/89/McWay_cove_1.jpg/330px-McWay_cove_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cove","wikidata":"Q31615"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Figure_lulworth_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a8/Figure_lulworth_formation.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Map showing two examples of how coves form. The rock types are those of Lulworth Cove. In example A, a river breaks through the resistant chalk back rock and limestone, leaving the weak clays to be rapidly eroded. In example B, the sea breaks through the limestone, perhaps by forming a cave, and then erodes the clay away.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFigure_lulworth_formation.png"}],"sounds":{"hidden":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b0/En-us-hidden.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/b/b0/En-us-hidden.ogg/En-us-hidden.ogg.mp3"}],"cove":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/86/EN-AU_ck1_cove.ogg?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/86/EN-AU_ck1_cove.ogg/EN-AU_ck1_cove.ogg.mp3"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey heron (00129p)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg/500px-Grey_heron_%2800129p%29.jpg","ratio":0.8691693290734824,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_heron_(00129p).jpg","share":0.586875},{"title":"Werner's nomenclature of colours greys","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg/500px-Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","ratio":0.794047619047619,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Werner%27s_nomenclature_of_colours_greys.jpg","share":0.320625},{"title":"Grey Carpet from above","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg/500px-Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg","share":0.166875},{"title":"Hidden Cove (8177726023)","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Hidden_Cove_%288177726023%29.jpg/500px-Hidden_Cove_%288177726023%29.jpg","ratio":1.4997631454287068,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hidden_Cove_(8177726023).jpg","share":0.16375},{"title":"Hidden Cove Craig y Gwbert - 